e best ones many other  countries the small countries in Europe  that have survived or have come out of  communism and are now new EU members  they have made reforms they have changed  turned around 180 degrees they have a  capital based pension system they have  flat taxes the EU is the biggest and  right now as it turns out the most  expensive piece project that we see and  eventually it will not keep peace it  will keep or it will start social unrest  so when these things pop up people will  rethink and the European Union as we  know it now will not exist in ten years  trust me  from a free market perspective and from  a very individualist perspective there  will be the rise of regions and there  will be competition among those regions  US policymakers can learn the following  from Europe  don't become Europe and don't don't  copy-paste our socialist solutions and  rather stick to the principles of the  founding fathers stick to your  constitution stick to individual freedom  the rule of law and really prevent your  citizens from big government  institutions from the fourth layer in  society from bureaucracy in again there  is no productivity in this and we can  only create growth and well-being for  everybody if we are productive  well our idea of helping people are  making them acquainted with free market  ideas is for example a free-market  Roadshow and this year we will tour 24  capitals starting in May in Tbilisi  going down to Turkey Greece and all the  countries ending up in in Spain and  Portugal at the end of June and what we  will discuss there with international  economists with business people with  opinion leaders is their charity  programs and the future of Europe  unemployment youth unemployment which is  a serious issue than teittleman's  generation and how to overcome this you  can find out about the free-market  Roadshow at WWF remarket /rs stuff
 

